<title>UK: UK regulator approves second weekly lottery draw.</title>
<headline>UK regulator approves second weekly lottery draw.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's National Lottery regulator Oflot said on Wednesday it had approved plans for Camelot Group Plc to run a second weekly draw.</p>
<p>The draw will take place on Wednesday and will include about six million stg to cover prizes.</p>
<p>The midweek lottery was expected to be launched some time next year.</p>
<p>The new draw reflects the growing popularity of Britain's National Lottery since its launch in November 1994.</p>
<p>Watching the main draw, which is televised live on Saturday night, has become a ritual for millions of Britons.</p>
<p>But it has proved less popular with bookmakers and soccer pools companies who argue that it has taken a large bite out of their profits.</p>
<p>Camelot is a consortium owned by Cadbury Schweppes Plc, GTECH Holdings Corp, De La Rue Plc and Racal Electronics Plc, which each have a 22.5 percent stake, and Japan's Fujitsu, which owns a 10 percent stake.</p>
